WEBVTT

01
00:00:05.002 --> 00:00:08.113
This is Pinned rows, a version of Value rows.

02
00:00:08.565 --> 00:00:14.809
Each row shows its value in a field. Stroke starts pinned, so its colors are already open.

03
00:00:15.311 --> 00:00:19.743
One click on green, and the stroke changes. There's no row to open first.

04
00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:25.330
Pin Background, and it stays open too. One more click for a light green background.

05
00:00:26.454 --> 00:00:31.311
Rows you don't pin open one at a time. Edges goes from round to sharp.

06
00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:40.403
Quick style says what it sets, and each style has a plain name, like Lines, Crossed lines and Filled.

07
00:00:42.164 --> 00:00:47.469
Now the next shape. The pinned rows are open for it too, so each change is one click.

08
00:00:49.214 --> 00:00:53.178
And the next one: two clicks again, and no row to open.

09
00:00:55.901 --> 00:01:00.569
A row you haven't pinned still opens on its own, beside the pinned ones.

10
00:01:02.682 --> 00:01:06.954
The full palette, with shades and a hex code, is one more click.

11
00:01:09.516 --> 00:01:14.798
Fill, Stroke style, Sloppiness and Opacity each open in place.

12
00:01:20.566 --> 00:01:24.017
Layers and the actions share one row of icons at the bottom.

13
00:01:26.034 --> 00:01:37.256
What works well: the rows you change most stay one click away, for every shape you select. Pins stay in place, so nothing jumps, and everything else stays a short summary.

14
00:01:37.958 --> 00:01:48.739
What's harder: every row carries a pin, so the panel is a little wider, and two pinned color rows make it taller. If you never pin anything, only Stroke stays open.
